### Data that is NOT stored

- No IP addresses.
- No device fingerprints.
- No analytics events (in v1; see exclusions).
- No user accounts, email addresses or passwords.
- No data on any server.
- No cookies (except a strictly necessary local storage flag for save/resume, which contains no personal data).

### Data lifecycle

- Data is created in the browser's IndexedDB when the user begins Stage 1.
- Data persists until the user explicitly deletes it (a "Delete all my data" button is available in the session menu and on the completion screen).
- Data is never transmitted anywhere.
- If the user clears browser data, the session is lost. The completion screen warns: "Your information is stored only in this browser on this device. If you clear your browser data, it will be lost. Export any documents you want to keep."
- No automatic expiry. Data persists until deleted by the user or by browser data clearing.

