## 6. Take-Forward Outputs

Six outputs. Each is a self-contained document. Each can be generated independently. Each is print-ready (A4, clean typography, no navigation elements, no URLs except the product name for reference). Each can be saved as PDF via the browser's print-to-PDF function.

### Output 1 — Heart Risk Audit Record

**What it is:** A structured summary of everything the user recorded in Stage 2: known conditions, medications, results, symptoms, family/shared history, lifestyle notes, documents available.

**User problem solved:** The user has a single, organised document containing everything they know. They can refer to it, update it, and use it as a personal health record for this topic.

**Format:** One to three pages. Sectioned by category. Each section headed clearly. Free-text entries reproduced as written. Gaps shown as "[Not recorded]" or "[Not known]". A header states: "This is a personal record, not a clinical document. It was created using Clarify heart risk."

**Privacy behaviour:** Generated for the user's own use. Contains all recorded information including the private note. Not designed for sharing. If the user prints it, they control who sees it. The document footer states: "This document contains personal health information. Keep it safe."

**Required / Conditional:** Required output (always available for generation).

**Standalone test:** A health professional reading this document without access to Clarify should understand what it is, who it concerns, what is recorded, and what is not recorded.

### Output 2 — Missing-Information Summary

**What it is:** A structured list of everything the user does not know, has not recorded, or is uncertain about, categorised as "You may be able to find this" or "Ask the health team."

**User problem solved:** The user can see, at a glance, what is missing. They can act on the "find this yourself" items before an appointment, reducing wasted time. They can see what questions the health team will need to answer.

**Format:** One to two pages. Two columns or two sections: "Things you can look into" and "Things to discuss with a health team." Priority items marked. A header states: "This summary was generated from information entered in Clarify heart risk. It is a prompt, not a clinical assessment."

**Privacy behaviour:** Contains derived health information (gaps imply what is known). Treated as personal. User controls sharing.

**Required / Conditional:** Required output.

### Output 3 — Health Team Discussion Brief

**What it is:** A one- to two-page document designed to be brought to a GP or specialist appointment. It summarises what is known, what is unclear, what questions the user has, and what they want from the conversation.

**User problem solved:** The user walks into an appointment prepared. They do not forget questions. They can hand the brief to the clinician or use it as their own prompt. The clinician gets a structured overview without the user having to narrate everything from memory.

**Format:** One to two pages. Sections: "About this person" (basic details, as selected by user), "What is known" (conditions, medications, relevant results — as selected), "What is unclear or missing" (gaps, as selected), "Questions for the health team" (as recorded), "What I would like from this conversation" (optional free text added at Stage 4). Header: "This brief was prepared using Clarify heart risk to support a conversation with a health team. It is not a clinical referral or assessment." Footer: space for the clinician to write notes if the user wishes.

**Privacy behaviour:** This is the primary shareable output. The user explicitly selects what is included via toggles in Stage 4. The user explicitly confirms before generation. The document does not include the private note, the user's own health information (if working for someone else), or any data the user has excluded. The document header does not include the user's name unless the user adds it.

**Required / Conditional:** Required output.

**Standalone test:** A GP receiving this document cold should understand who it concerns, what is known, what is unclear, and what the patient wants to discuss, without needing to access Clarify or any other resource.

### Output 4 — Decision and Next-Action Record

**What it is:** A record of what was discussed, what was decided, and what happens next. Completed in Stage 5 after a health team conversation, or as a record of intentions if no conversation has taken place.

**User problem solved:** The user has a written record of decisions and actions. They do not have to rely on memory. They can refer to it when arranging follow-up, picking up prescriptions, or attending the next appointment.

**Format:** One page. Sections: "Date of conversation" (or "Not yet had"), "What was discussed," "What was decided or recommended," "Next steps," "Follow-up appointment" (if known). Header: "This is a personal record of a health team conversation, created using Clarify heart risk. It is the user's own record, not an official clinical note."

**Privacy behaviour:** Personal record. Contains health information. User controls sharing.

**Required / Conditional:** Required output.

### Output 5 — People You Love Follow-up

**What it is:** A short record for the user who was working on behalf of someone they love. It captures: what the user needs to tell or discuss with that person, what that person needs to do, any follow-up the user intends, and any boundaries the user wants to maintain.

**User problem solved:** When helping someone else, the helper often forgets what they meant to pass on, or feels uncertain about what is their business and what is not. This output gives them a private prompt.

**Format:** Half a page to one page. Sections: "Things to discuss with [name/this person]," "Things they may need to do," "My follow-up intentions," "Boundaries and notes to self." Header: "This is a private note for the person who created it. It is not intended to be shared unless the creator chooses to."

**Privacy behaviour:** Explicitly private to the user. Not included in any other output. Not shareable by design (the user can print it and hand it to someone, but the tool does not generate a "shareable version" of this document).

**Required / Conditional:** Conditional — generated only if the user was working for someone they love.

### Output 6 — Clarify Take-Forward Pack

**What it is:** A single combined PDF containing any or all of the above outputs, selected by the user, in a logical order, with a cover page.

**User problem solved:** The user wants one document, not five separate files. They want to print it once, put it in a folder, and have everything in one place.

**Format:** Cover page: "Clarify heart risk — Take-Forward Pack. Prepared [date]. For [name/the person I am working for]." Then the selected outputs in order: Heart Risk Audit Record → Missing-Information Summary → Health Team Discussion Brief → Decision and Next-Action Record → People You Love Follow-up (if applicable). Each output starts on a new page. The cover page includes a note: "This pack was created using Clarify heart risk (heartfirst.shyntesy.com/clarify). It is a personal working document, not a clinical record."

**Privacy behaviour:** The user selects which outputs to include. The pack inherits the privacy settings of each included output. The private note is never included. The People You Love Follow-up is included only if the user explicitly selects it (it is unchecked by default).

**Required / Conditional:** Required output (available whenever at least one other output has been generated).

### Output format specifications (all outputs)

- A4 portrait.
- System font stack (no web font dependency for print).
- Minimum 12pt body text.
- Clear section headings.
- No background colours that waste ink.
- No navigation elements, buttons, links or interactive elements.
- Page numbers in footer.
- Product name and URL in header or footer for reference.
- Date of generation.
- Print CSS hides all non-content elements.
- Each output is a single HTML view that can be printed or saved as PDF via the browser.

