## 7. Privacy and Sharing Behaviour

### Core principle

All data stays on the user's device. No data is transmitted to any server. No analytics, no tracking, no telemetry in v1.

### Separation of identifying and health information

The information model separates:

- **Identifying information:** preferred name, relationship, age, sex. Stored in the Person entity.
- **Health and private information:** conditions, medications, results, symptoms, family history, lifestyle notes, gaps, questions, outcomes, private notes. Stored in the HealthInformation and WorkingNotes entities.

These are stored in the same local database (IndexedDB) because they are on the same device and the user controls the device. However, they are structurally separate so that:

- Shareable outputs (Discussion Brief) can be generated from health information without including identifying information the user has not explicitly approved.
- The private note is structurally excluded from all shareable outputs. It is a separate field that no output template references.
- If the user is working for "Both," Person A's health information and Person B's health information are in separate records. They are never combined in a single output unless the user explicitly selects a combined view.

### User-controlled sharing

The user decides what is shared, at the point of output generation:

1. The user selects which output to generate.
2. For the Discussion Brief, the user toggles which sections to include.
3. The user previews the output before printing or saving.
4. No output is generated automatically. No output is sent anywhere.

### What the tool does NOT claim

The tool does not describe itself as "secure," "encrypted," "protected" or "safe." These terms imply technical guarantees that are not implemented in a local-first, no-server application. The tool states plainly:

- "Your information stays in this browser on this device."
- "If you clear your browser data, your information will be lost."
- "No one else can access it unless they access this device or this browser."
- "You control what you print, save or share."

### Data deletion

- A "Delete all my data" button is available in the session menu (persistent, accessible from any stage) and on the completion screen.
- Clicking it shows a confirmation: "This will permanently delete all information you have entered in this session. This cannot be undone. Export any documents you want to keep before deleting."
- On confirmation, all IndexedDB records for the session are deleted.
- There is no "soft delete" or "trash." Deletion is immediate and permanent.

### Browser and device considerations

- The completion screen and the orientation text note: "Your information is stored in this browser on this device. It will not sync to another device or browser. If you use private/incognito browsing, your information will be lost when you close the window."
- The tool detects private/incognito mode (where possible) and warns the user at the start of Stage 1: "You appear to be in a private browsing session. Your information will not be saved after you close this window. Consider using a normal browser window if you want to save and resume."

