## 10. Deliberate Exclusions from Version One

| Exclusion | Reason | Revisit when |
|---|---|---|
| User accounts and server-side storage | Adds complexity, privacy obligations (GDPR data controller responsibilities), and infrastructure cost. Local-first meets the v1 requirement. | If users consistently lose data by clearing browser storage, or if cross-device access becomes a strong demand. |
| "Someone I love" and "Both" paths | Designed in full (see Sections 3–6) but not built in the vertical slice. Building the self-directed path first validates the core experience. | Immediately after the vertical slice is validated. This is the first addition, not a distant future item. |
| Email or cloud export of outputs | Would require server infrastructure, email handling, and create a data-transmission point that contradicts the local-first principle. | If user research shows strong demand. Would require a privacy reassessment. |
| Analytics and usage tracking | Contradicts the privacy-conscious principle. No data leaves the device. | If the founder decides anonymised, consent-based usage data is needed for product development. Would require explicit, informed consent and a privacy notice. |
| Multi-language support | v1 is UK/International English. | When there is evidence of demand for other languages. |
| Clinical risk scoring or algorithms | Clarify is explicitly not a diagnostic or risk-calculation tool. | Never. This is a permanent exclusion. |
| Integration with GP systems, patient portals or electronic health records | Would require API access, clinical governance, data controller agreements, and significant regulatory compliance. | Not in the foreseeable roadmap. |
| Automatic reminders or follow-up prompts | Would require server infrastructure or notification permissions. Contradicts local-first principle. | If a lightweight, local-only reminder (e.g., "You noted a follow-up in 3 months") is feasible without server support. |
| Combined Take-Forward Pack | Individual outputs are built first. The pack is a convenience wrapper. | After individual outputs are validated. Low-effort addition. |
| Appointment-arranging script and "What to expect" guidance | Useful but not essential to the core value. | Second build iteration. |
| Payment integration | The sales page (shyntesy.com/clarify) handles purchase. Clarify itself does not process payment. The application URL is provided after purchase. Payment mechanism is a sales-page concern, not a product concern. | N/A — handled externally. |

