- the user problem it solves;
- why it is needed;
- what output it contributes to;
- whether it is required or conditional;
- what happens when the user does not know the answer;
- whether it concerns the user, someone they love, or both;
- what privacy or sharing issue applies;
- what unnecessary burden it may create.

No field has been included without this justification. No field exists "because it might be useful." Every field earns its place by contributing to a specific output that the user can hold, print, share or keep.

